  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum number of lone pairs of electron on the central atom from the following species is ......<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClO</mi><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><msup><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msup></msub></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi>ClO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup></math>:&nbsp;The central atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>, there is one lone pair of electrons on the central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>:&nbsp;The central atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math>. It has two lone pair on central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>:&nbsp;The central atom is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math>. It contains one lone pair on central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup></math>:&nbsp;It contains three lone pair on central atom.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0078_4f2b85a9d9ba.png\" style=\"width: 278px; height: 279px;\" /></p>"
  }
